t the Young Prince aegon a suitable  match for renera this isn't uncommon in  the Targaryen family viserys's parents  Balon and Alyssa were brother and sister  and so were his grandparents jaharas and  alisane Lionel also offers another match  which the king first thinks is Lionel's  own son Harwin break bones considered  the strongest man in the Seven Kingdoms  but it's actually rhaenice and corliss's  eldest son Leonor Valerian it's arguably  the most practical match the valerians  are a Noble House extremely affluent and  a match would do well to mend the  relationship between Targaryen and  Valerian after the king chose not to Wed  their daughter Elena but if Ranier is to  wedling or he must first survive the  fighting in the stepsons I also want to  make quick mention that we haven't  really seen if the king's sickness has  gotten any worse we saw both his back  and fingers suffer from a mysterious  incurable ailment so expect that to make  a return in future episodes rhaenyra and  Kristen camp for the night where renera  asks if the realm will ever accept her  as Queen she's probably thinking about  what her aunt said last episode that men  would rather see the realm put to the  torch than see a woman sit on the throne  Kristen doesn't have the best response  saying that the realm will be forced to  accept her but before the conversation  can continue they're attacked by a wild  boar and Rainier just lets out all this  pent-up rage killing it years of  betrayal frustration and anger poured  into every stroke of her blade a drunk  King viserys lemons his current  predicament he's being pressured from  all sides to name aegon as Heir which  would mean spurning his daughter for the  king so wanted his son he became  obsessed with it believing this  obsession is what would eventually kill  his dearest Emma he thought naming  renera as Heir was the right thing to do  after all he didn't think he'd remarry  and have a son no less so maybe his  dream of having a boy 