han done the King has sent a  messenger to dwarf Stone one of these  smaller Islands Corliss and Damon used  to launch their Siege of Bloodstone in  this letter the King has decided to  offer aid but that Aid will take some  time in order to get there Rainier sits  with her father coincidentally in the  chair reserved for the hand of the king  she can't help but feel like a pawn just  a bargaining chip her father can use to  sell for a fleet of ships or a mountain  stronghold Ranier even says that the  Lords of the realm gather to Feast on  the bones of her carcass which is pretty  much what viserys said after the death  of his wife and son visiris knows what  it's like to be in rhaenyra's position  Emma was a fine choice for him because  she was an Aaron of the veil and they  had an army which would rival that of  the north however in this case it worked  for for the king as he ended up falling  in love with her you know when he's not  cutting babies out of her so the king  wanting to see rhaenyra contented gives  her the choice on who to marry hoping  that her choice will strengthen her  claim to the throne and Shore up her  secession and she seems pretty happy  with this decision the scene ends with a  promise on her mother's memory that she  will not be supplanted it seems the  wavering he was having a few nights ago  has subsided and he is firmly stuck by  his choice the Final Act of the episode  revolves around the siege of Bloodstone  and it is not going well even though we  can see Damon flying around on caraxis  the crap feeder and his forces merely  Retreat into the caves whenever the  dragon comes near essentially making  them useless with food and men running  low and help weeks away something must  be done or defeat is inevitable vaiman  believes the problem is Damon going so  far as to say if the king won't even  help him why should they but Corliss  quickly quiets his brother he won't have  any Mutiny here as demon arrives so too  does the king's a messenger giving demon  word that his brother is to ride with 10  ships and 2 000 men for Damon this is  the worst possible news the whole point  of him and his campaign in the  stepstones was to prove himself without  the help of his brother that's why he  takes his rage out on the messenger and  volunteers himself as bait to lure the  triarchy forces from their caves Damon  arrives alone on Bloodstone offering a  white flag of surrender and his sword  Dark sister as a sign of defeat but  kragistrahar isn't stupid he checks the  skies for dragons and sends only a few  men at a time to retrieve the prince the  whole thing is a wildly dangerous dare  say heroic aroos in order to get crab  feeder's men out of their holes and it  actually works Damon goes on a rampage  but is soon shot down by multiple arrows  pinned against the worn out Hull of a  wrecked ship sensing the Rogue Prince is  on his last legs the crab feeder sends  out the last of his men which will prove  to be a fatal Mr stake the diversion has  allowed corliss's men to ride ashore and  more importantly the dragon sea smoke to  make quick work of the enemy surrounding  Damon sea smoke is now the Third Dragon  we've been introduced to thus far only  14 more to go he's written by Lenor  Valerian who you'll recall has Targaryen  blood being the son of renice from this  point it basically becomes a crispy  bloodbath and under the combined  pressure of the Valerian forces and a  dragon the triarchy forces are defeated  Damon wants crab feeder's head and  pursues him into the caves we don't  actually see them fight but honestly I  was okay with that we just got this  beautiful action sequence and I was fine  with not seeing them duke it out it also  lines up with a book that simply states  crab feeder was slain by Damon in  single-handed combat with his sword Dark  sister the only difference was that he  was beheaded I also love this shot of  Damon next to this treasure as he  himself holds on to his treasure t